    },
    {
      "id": "UH9sy1eFAzEh_DMxFusFJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -950.5570742289219,
      "y": 2478.5831298828125,
      "width": 2176.77880859375,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3uV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 899654156,
      "version": 1065,
      "versionNonce": 307583116,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793889915023,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Streamlit creates a thread and accepts a question or PDF. PDF bytes are saved using a content hash, parsed page, split into overlapping chunks, embedded with BGE-M3, and added to a persistent FAISS index.\n2. Each user turn enters LangGraph as a HumanMessage. The Chatbot node predefine the system policy and calls the tool-enabled LLM. tools_condition routes tool calls to ToolNode, tool results return to the chatbot for\nsynthesis.\n3. For document questions, rag_tool retrieves the top=4 similar chunks and returns source/page metadata. Other tools cover web search, arithmetic, weather, stock quote, and a simulated purchase.\n4. SqliteSaver stores graph state per thread. A simulated purchase triggers interrupt(); Streamlit shows approval controls and resumes the same checkpoint with Command (resume=\"yes or \"no\").\n5. Evaluate a fixed question set across RAG version using answer relevancy, correcctness, Faithfulness, and contextual relevancy, analyze failures and repeat improvements.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "1Hwlng8_PB03II1v9zKox",
      "originalText": "1. Streamlit creates a thread and accepts a question or PDF. PDF bytes are saved using a content hash, parsed page, split into overlapping chunks, embedded with BGE-M3, and added to a persistent FAISS index.\n2. Each user turn enters LangGraph as a HumanMessage. The Chatbot node predefine the system policy and calls the tool-enabled LLM. tools_condition routes tool calls to ToolNode, tool results return to the chatbot for synthesis.\n3. For document questions, rag_tool retrieves the top=4 similar chunks and returns source/page metadata. Other tools cover web search, arithmetic, weather, stock quote, and a simulated purchase.\n4. SqliteSaver stores graph state per thread. A simulated purchase triggers interrupt(); Streamlit shows approval controls and resumes the same checkpoint with Command (resume=\"yes or \"no\").\n5. Evaluate a fixed question set across RAG version using answer relevancy, correcctness, Faithfulness, and contextual relevancy, analyze failures and repeat improvements.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
